variable {R : Type u} [Ring R]

local notation "DMod" => DerivedCategory (ModuleCat R)

/- Domain-style sampling for Proposition 15.79.3:
- primary domain: perfect and compact objects in the derived category `D(R)`;
- sampled owner declarations:
  `DerivedCategory.IsPerfect`,
  `IsCompactObject`,
  `ObjectProperty.IsStableUnderRetracts`,
  `preadditiveCoyoneda_hocolim_comparison_is_iso`;
- best owner abstractions:
  the proposition is `source-facing`, but its two predicates are already canonically owned by
  `DerivedCategory.IsPerfect` and `IsCompactObject`;
  the file should therefore keep only the source-facing equivalence for a fixed object and avoid
  importing proof-route bridge files as if they were part of the owner surface;
- primitive vs. derived:
  the only primitive datum here is the object `K : D(R)`;
  closure of compact objects under retracts and the represented-Hom hocolim comparison map are
  derived bridge API from neighboring owner files, not primitive data of this proposition file;
- source/core/bridge triage:
  `source-facing`: the equivalence for a fixed object `K`;
  `core/canonical`: `K.IsPerfect` and `IsCompactObject K`;
  `bridge/view`: the generator description of perfect objects, compact-object retract stability,
